@@ -641,6 +642,18 @@ Pi hides `subagent_done` for `auto-exit: true` agents. If you want an interactiv
 
 Use `caller_ping` when the child needs the parent. The child sends a message up, exits, and leaves a session file that the parent can resume.
 
+### Persistent interactive worker status and steering
+
+Set `interactive-status: true` only on an `interactive`, `auto-exit: false` worker. It retains its normal pane while reporting each settled Pi turn to its parent; incompatible launch or resume configuration fails clearly. The parent receives `subagents:status:v1` events with reachable pane, turn state (`running`, `settled`, or `error`), and active child/process counts. A quiet settled status (both counts are known zero) also wakes the parent with the latest assistant output; active or unknown work updates status without waking a stop review. `activeProcesses` is zero when no `process` tool is active, otherwise Pi queries the documented `pi-processes` list callback and reports `unknown` if no provider answers.
+
+While the worker is reachable and its latest status is quiet and `settled`, the parent can call:
+
+```text
+subagent_steer({ id, text })
+```
+
+`text` may be multiline. The tool atomically queues a message for that child run; the child calls Pi's supported `sendUserMessage` API when idle. It never types into the terminal editor, so a human draft remains untouched. Its result means queued only, not child acceptance or execution; wait for a following status before treating it as executed. Queue items are run-id scoped and are not replayed by a resumed worker. A parent `/reload` retains and reattaches an opted-in worker in the same Pi process; a full parent exit still follows `parent-close-policy`.
+
 ## Resuming child sessions
 
 `subagent_resume` starts an existing child session again. You can pass a follow-up task.
